  message: "VALIDATION BAKEOFF (2026-07-19) — gate is REAL but INCOMPLETE on real code; stays violated. Surveyed real repos w/ final merged code (scratchpad/inv-fahub/*.json). CLEAN: Scala(docspell) 0 magnets, gate fired 5692, 38 recovered. NEAR-CLEAN: Swift(vernissage) 6 candidate magnets/100 binds (need legit-vs-real check), gate fired 2084, 81 recovered. NOT CLEAN: Go(caddy) 41 magnets/666 binds gate-fired-1 (Dispenser.Val<-53, Next<-46 = d.Val() UNTYPED-RECEIVER method calls @0.85); Rust(ripgrep) 23 magnets gate-fired-2; D(dub) 9 FREE-FORM magnets (writeln<-70/to<-33/execute<-15 stdlib calls misbinding to internal methods). ROOT CAUSE: the fleet workflow gated each analyzer BARE-IDENTIFIER free-call path; synthetic+adversarial tests validated THAT path; but INV-fahub funnel is UNTYPED-RECEIVER method calls, which for Go/Rust resolve via a SEPARATE method/selector path never gated. D free-form path also ungated (D excluded from fleet PR as done). Scala/Swift clean because WI-bihit/votar gated the untyped-receiver path directly. Owner: CHECKPOINT/bank finding. See follow-up WI for the corrective per-language pass."  # 785a
- op: discuss  # 967c
  at: '2026-07-19T09:30:48Z'  # 967c
  by: agent  # 967c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 967c
  clock: 6  # 967c
  nonce: 967c  # 967c
  message: "REFRAME + DEFER (2026-07-19, autonomous). The bakeoff's magnet counts (Rust 439 / D 266 / Go 41 / ...) were substantially MEASUREMENT ARTIFACTS. The receiver-blind-magnet detector over-counted three FP classes: (1) typed-receiver resolutions (go.py: every internal method-resolution requires a typed receiver -> the '41' were typed_receiver FPs); (2) scoped/static calls (Rust Type::new/from - explicit target type, correctly resolved); (3) same-class generic/template calls (C++ AP4_Array<T>::x -> AP4_Array::x, flagged only on the <T> notation mismatch). Detector hardened this session: hypergumbo_core/receiver_blind_magnets.py excludes receiver-marker + resolution_quality edges, adds a receiver='qualified' exclusion for explicit-type calls (detector-side ready; per-analyzer marking is the remaining accuracy work), and normalizes generic/template owner names.\n\nRe-measured (current detector, min_conf 0.80): D=0 high-conf (all binds <=0.77); Go~0 genuine; Rust=dominated by scoped Type::new FPs + a macro path (Rust is rust-analyzer's PARKED domain, WI-gojum); C++(bento4)=285 GENUINE cross-class receiver-blind binds BUT ALL fanout-1 (no target with >=2 callers) -> NO magnet concentration.\n\nCONCLUSION: the 'magnet crisis' (dozens of sites collapsing onto one arbitrary method, poisoning centrality) does NOT occur in the fleet - that severity was artifact. Genuine residual = scattered single-call-site receiver-blind binds (mild precision issue). INV-fahub stays 'violated' (per-edge letter IS violated) but practical severity is low.\n\nDECISION: fully crushing = gating the scattered residual across 8+ tree-sitter analyzers (large, low-value grind), and ADR-0012 (multi-fidelity / type-resolved) is the documented RIGHT fix, deliberately deferred. So INV-fahub is DEFERRED to the very end of Wave 5. Remaining work when resumed: per-analyzer receiver='qualified' marking (detector honesty) + optional residual gating. Merged this session: the scip-edge endpoint fix (9266762d4b) + detector hardening + template normalization."  # 967c
